<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reza Qoli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">blinded <a href="/years/1741">1741</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reza Qoli was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>, and served for a time as a regent and commander. In 1741 Nader had him blinded on suspicion of involvement in a conspiracy against his life. Accounts of the Afsharid Empire cite this act as an example of the paranoia and cruelty of Nader's later years, which hastened the decline of the empire's administrative coherence.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The growing suspicion and cruelty of Nader's later years, including the blinding of his eldest son <b>Reza Qoli</b> in 1742 on suspicion of plotting an assassination attempt, accelerated the decay of whatever administrative coherence the empire possessed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
